    "domain": "Include a person only if a historically significant part of that person's contribution is directly to the design, construction, testing, analysis or improvement of machines, structures, engines, vehicles, aircraft, spacecraft, ships, power systems, electrical and communication systems, industrial processes, manufacturing systems, control systems, nuclear reactors, or the instruments, production methods and engineering methods used to build and operate them; qualifying contributions include mechanical engineering and machine design, civil and structural engineering, electrical and power engineering, electronics and communications engineering, aeronautical and aerospace engineering, chemical and process engineering, marine and automotive engineering, control and systems engineering, industrial and manufacturing engineering, and nuclear engineering. Reject anyone whose principal significance lies in any other field. Reject physicists, chemists and materials scientists whose work lacks a central engineering contribution embodied in a machine, structure, process, system or engineering method; mathematicians and theoretical mechanicians whose significance is analytical rather than tied to engineered systems; computer scientists and software researchers whose principal contribution is to computation, algorithms or software rather than physical systems; architects whose significance lies primarily in architectural design, aesthetics or planning rather than structural engineering; geologists, geophysicists, mining geologists and prospectors whose principal work concerns Earth science or resource discovery rather than engineering; physicians, biologists and life scientists without a substantive engineering contribution; industrial designers and craft practitioners whose significance is aesthetic or artisanal rather than engineering; industrialists, financiers, company founders and executives whose importance is primarily commercial or organisational rather than technical; military commanders, pilots, navigators and explorers whose significance lies in operating or using engineered systems rather than creating or materially improving them; and inventors of consumer novelties whose work lacks substantial engineering design, analysis or technological significance.",
